(7416367, 1169149, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I think DPC voters are chronically allergic to techniques involving stuff like zoomblur, long exposure, subject tracking...they seem to lerve their images clean, sharply focused and usually saturated to death. *cough cough a certain primarily seascape photog*<br/> <br/>Anyway I think that''s the main problem here, cause I can feel myself running alongside or just behind Joie, trying to keep up with an unleashed dog running and shooting at the same time!  Maybe the light is a teeny bit on the blown-out side; the dog''s face, were it towards us, would probably have helped this image score higher. Comp and lighting are suitable for the subject.<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I think DPC voters are chronically allergic to techniques involving stuff like zoomblur, long exposure, subject tracking...they seem to lerve their images clean, sharply focused and usually saturated to death. *cough cough a certain primarily seascape photog* Anyway I think that''s the main problem here, cause I can feel myself running alongside or just behind Joie, trying to keep up with an unleashed dog running and shooting at the same time!  Maybe the light is a teeny bit on the blown-out side; the dog''s face, were it towards us, would probably have helped this image score higher. Comp and lighting are suitable for the subject. Hope this has been helpful Susan', '2015-11-15 18:12:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7416961, 1168718, 96751, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous image, Glen. And an awesome finish for a free study.<br/> <br/>In future image, you can add notes and comments under your image by clicking on the "Edit the details of the image" link under the image in the left column.</td>', 'Gorgeous image, Glen. And an awesome finish for a free study. In future image, you can add notes and comments under your image by clicking on the "Edit the details of the image" link under the image in the left column.', '2015-11-17 22:34:00.000000', NULL, 0),
