(7418365, 1169019, 86447, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is a lovely scene, Frank!<br/> <br/>I love how you''ve composed this and included that loving couple to give it a "story".<br/> <br/>The sun being about on the "Thirds" makes this extra pleasing.<br/> <br/>I find myself wishing that third person weren''t interrupting "my couple"... I''ve already bought into them as mine when he arrives...  Perhaps if you''d waited until he''s passed by?<br/> <br/>There is a great amount of noise/breakdown in the image... and some really odd yellow coloring around the limbs upper right that I think lowered the scores from the voters.  And I agree with giantmike that the saturation is a bit higher than I would expect the colors to be naturally.<br/> <br/>Thanks for entering this... I hope you''ll continue, Frank.  <br/> <br/>It''s good to have you here at DPC!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is a lovely scene, Frank! I love how you''ve composed this and included that loving couple to give it a "story". The sun being about on the "Thirds" makes this extra pleasing. I find myself wishing that third person weren''t interrupting "my couple"... I''ve already bought into them as mine when he arrives...  Perhaps if you''d waited until he''s passed by? There is a great amount of noise/breakdown in the image... and some really odd yellow coloring around the limbs upper right that I think lowered the scores from the voters.  And I agree with giantmike that the saturation is a bit higher than I would expect the colors to be naturally. Thanks for entering this... I hope you''ll continue, Frank.   It''s good to have you here at DPC! ', '2015-11-24 19:07:33.000000', NULL, 0),
